<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A2.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Our reward gradually upgrade and reach converge.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.SS2.tab1" class="ltx_table">
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The hyperparameters used for the agent are detailed in Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.2 Training Details ‣ Appendix B Experiment Setup Details ‣ Reinforced Visual Perception with Tools" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. During training with the veRL framework, we observed a degradation in the response quality when batch-inferencing with Qwen2.5-VL by vllm as the batch size increased. Consequently, we imposed a limit on the batch size used for each inference step.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T7" class="ltx_table">
